  "question": {
    "text": "The solubility product of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The solubility of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></math> solution is&nbsp; &nbsp; ------<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>(nearest integer).<br />Given: Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>233</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "233",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>For the insoluble salt barium sulphate, sulphate ion added is the common ion. Due to the common&nbsp;ion effect the solubility of barium sulphate decreases. Let us assume solubility of barium sulphate is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8652;</mo><munder><msup><mi>Ba</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></munder><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><munder><msubsup><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo>&#10230;</mo><munder><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><munder><msubsup><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi>SP</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msup><mi>Ba</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mfenced><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msubsup><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8771;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>gL</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p></blockquote>",
